hey friends welcome back to the deep  dive snippet this is a clip from my  conversation with julian hearn the  founder of the 250 million dollar  company huel and here we're talking  about the idea of company culture and  how to keep people in your own company  in your own team happy healthy and  productive so if you're a manager or  leader of any kind then hopefully you'll  find this useful how do you how do you  think about things like culture like  culture is one of these big words  everyone everyone talks about yeah  what's the sort of culture that you're  trying to make it heal and i guess how  do you  how do you mold it in that direction so  i think culture is yeah i think it's  uh super super important and super  important to give it to you care and  attention it will happen naturally  but i think uh the hardest culture will  probably be a company that's been  existing for a very long time i've  worked to places and once you've got a  culture it's very hard to change that  culture luckily with your because i  started with a blank sheet of paper  and i was a founder and i was there i  think it's been fairly  easy to do in some ways because  i didn't start this company just to make  money i wanted something i was really  proud of i wanted a company where i was  going to work there as well so it's very  easy to sort of say i want to work  somewhere where i'm yeah there's no  dicks i want to work place where people  are nice  and i want but i want to perform i want  to get good results to create a culture  where um we we are you know market  leader we achieve great things but we  don't burn people out and people don't  want to leave every two years because  it's such a soul-destroyed place to work  you know they they don't there's no  fights there's no crying in the office  you don't want any of that so we want to  really look after people but we don't  want to have we want to have that energy  and that that sort of passion to achieve  great things and so have higher targets  so try to merge those two together so  sort of stuff that we do is we do  recruit well i think that we do  have ambitious targets but not not so  ambitious you're never going to achieve  any of them  um  we do look after people we have a people  team  that people team look after the team and  make sure there's anybody with any  problems we do provide a lot of perks  she always got share options  quite generous share options as well  and so again we're all  hopefully  more on the level playing field together  and rolling in the same direction  and then we do lots of additional perks  like we've got gym at work we bring in  the pt we have  you know free shield around the office i  went to a posh office the other day a  very  rich company they're charging one pound  eighty for a coffee don't have to do it  you know even stuff like that i think  makes a difference we've you know we  really try and think about doing the  right thing at all times nice  that's really cool yeah i think that's  one thing we're starting to think about  a lot harder now that the team has sort  of sort of accidentally become 17 people  who are like all right now we need to  really think hard about this culture  thing and have you written anything down  uh we've got core values and stuff but  they're all very rough first drafty but  no we haven't really really written down  any cultural principles yeah i would  start it yeah just think about what it  is and words that you may use and  phrases you may use just write it down i  mean i couldn't probably could send you  my first deck that i did it's pretty  crude and pretty rough we've refined it  made it better but there's there's very  famous culture decks out there i think  that um netflix one is one that's often  used very long now it's probably a bit  too long maybe a bit too specific if you  looked at the netflix one did a crude  version of that a quick crude version um  talk about you know principles some  stuff  stuff you don't want to do the stuff you  do want to do um  but yeah so we have two sets we have uh  in terms of values we have uh shaw's  dna's us as a company so nutrition first  tastes the close second  and then we have how to be a huligan  which is what we sort of call all of our  customers and all of our employees will  be hugh ligands and there'll be stuff in  there like  number one  is uh make customers happy number two is  don't be a dick stuff like that  sick  um any time sorry just one other thing  on that is um  i still induct everybody comes into the  business and i think that it's very easy  for a culture deck to become dusty put  in a draw nobody sees it  so what we've done is that when  everybody joins i do it so i'll induct  everybody who joins  and  give them my thoughts on culture from my  perspective  so don't be a dick's like you know don't  don't gossip around the office no that's  not allowed i don't accept that if i  hear that you'd be in big trouble  we print out those two sets of values on  just a little sticker everybody's laptop  in the business should have it on stick  it on there when they first join so at  least it sort of tries to keep it top of  mind  and then um  you know then you've got to live it you  have to live those so you don't want to  work right sort of flaky stuff that's  a bit aloof never gonna happen  so just try and remember and try and  quote those things back to somebody if  they're doing something wrong and try  and you know make sure you try and yeah  bring them to life and  it's very easy i think it's healed to a  certain extent we don't have a flaw  which is just from management you know  like james and this our ceo myself we  all sit you know open plan offices all  sit together and try and sort of live  those values together  awesome yeah i think when i first  started out the business though i i i i  came across things like culture and like  values and missions i was like oh what  is this [ __ ] but now i'm like oh  crap i really wish i had paid more  attention to this yeah hey friends thank  you so much for watching if you enjoyed  this clip then click here for the full  unedited episode and if you like that  then do please consider subscribing to  the channel it means a lot thank you so  much and have a great day

